{
  "contributes": [
    // GITHUB COPILOT AS A PROVIDER, SELECTABLE WITH NO DECLARATION (providers.md, "A provider the
    // agent has built in"; docs/design/pi-codex-provider-shadowing.md BI-D14): the provider and a
    // profile over it, the way packs/openai-auth ships `openai-codex` and `codex`. packs/copilot
    // needs this pack, so selecting the Copilot CLI brings it; selected without copilot, beside
    // pi, it makes `-p pi=github-copilot` and the mixed set
    // `"profile": {"pi": ["bedrock", "github-copilot"]}` work with nothing in the user's config.
    //
    // The provider names no endpoint and no credential. An agent that has it built in (pi,
    // opencode, oh-omp: their `built_in_providers`) runs it on its own client, list and login. The
    // Copilot CLI runs it on its own GitHub login: its pack needs this one, and a pack binds a
    // platform by needing a pack that ships a provider of it. The `platform` is the one fact the
    // provider offers about itself, so an agent with no GitHub Copilot client of its own (claude,
    // codex) is told a bare `-p github-copilot` reaches nothing for it, rather than staying on its
    // own login as if the profile re-pointed it. The profile is `github-copilot`, not `copilot`,
    // which names the Copilot CLI agent in `-p copilot=...`.
    {
      "kind": "provider",
      "name": "github-copilot",
      "platform": "github-copilot"
    },
    {
      "kind": "profile",
      "name": "github-copilot",
      "provider": "github-copilot"
    }
  ],
  "description": "GitHub Copilot as one provider and profile: the Copilot CLI's own login, and the GitHub Copilot client pi, opencode and oh-omp have built in. It installs nothing; the copilot pack brings it, and you may select it without copilot.",
  "name": "github-copilot"
}
